  "worked_solution": "The given points are ${{(1,4)}_{\u23df}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{1},\\,{y}_{1})},$ ${{(a,b)}_{\u23df}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{2},\\,{y}_{2})}$ and ${{(3,5)}_{\u23df}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{m},\\,{y}_{m})}\\,.$\n\nWe use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}_{m},{y}_{m}) & =(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2}) \\\\ (3,5) & =(\\frac{1+a}{2},\\frac{4+b}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding $x$- and $y$-coordinates in the equation above gives us\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}3=\\frac{1+a}{2} \\\\ 5=\\frac{4+b}{2}\\end{aligned}\\,\u21d2\\,{\\begin{aligned}a=5 \\\\ b=6.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $(a,b)=(5,6)$ and $a+b=11.$",
